Explanation of what each does:

- In **TileGroup**:
  - We pull `required` out of the props.
  - We pass that single `required={required}` down into every `<RadioTile>` child.
  - We put `position: relative` on the `<fieldset>` so that the absolutely-positioned inputs are anchored to the outline of the group.
- In **RadioTile**:
  - We augment the public `RadioTileProps` to accept a `required?: boolean`.
  - We destructure it from `...rest` and pass it to the hidden `<input>` as well as applying the inline style  
    `style={{ position: 'absolute', bottom: 0, left: '50%' }}` so the browser’s validation bubble appears at the bottom center of the tile group.

With these in place you can now write:

```jsx
<TileGroup name="foo" required>
  <RadioTile value="a">A</RadioTile>
  <RadioTile value="b">B</RadioTile>
  <RadioTile value="c">C</RadioTile>
</TileGroup>
```

and the native “Please select one of these options” tooltip will appear centered at the bottom of the group.
